# Feature modules

- Put each domain under `frontend/features/<kebab-name>/` using `api/`, `hooks/`, `components/`, and `types/` as needed.
- `app/**/page.tsx` files should stay thin: import a single feature entry component (e.g. `ProjectsPage`, `SystemStatusPage`). Do not call backend APIs directly from `app/` routes.
- Shared layout chrome lives in `frontend/components/admin/`. Shared HTTP utilities live in `frontend/lib/api/` (e.g. `client.ts` with `apiRequest`, `apiUrl`).
- Naming: API modules `*Api.ts`, hooks `use*.ts`, colocated types under `types/`.

## Adding a feature

1. Create `frontend/features/<name>/` with the API module calling `apiRequest` / `apiUrl` only.
2. Add `frontend/app/<route>/page.tsx` that composes the feature root component.
3. Register the route in `frontend/config/adminNav.ts` and rely on `AdminSidebar` for navigation.
